.TH CJSON_CLONE 3 "2026-07-10" "c_collections" "C Collections Library - Functions"
.SH NAME
cjson_clone \- deep-copy a DOM subtree
.SH LIBRARY
C Collections (libccollections, \-lccollections)
.SH SYNOPSIS
.nf
#include <cjson.h>

cjson cjson_clone(cjson node);
.fi
.SH DESCRIPTION
.nf
Returns a fully independent copy of the subtree rooted at node.
All strings are duplicated, all arrays and objects are recursively
cloned.  The clone uses the same allocator as the source (taken from
the root node's stored m_procs).
.fi
.SH RETURN VALUE
.nf
New root node on success (caller owns it), or NULL on allocation failure.
.fi
.SH "SEE ALSO"
.BR cjson_destroy (3)
